          "filename": "Former Albert Street station, Cork - geograph.org.uk - 76470.jpg",
          "caption": "Former Albert Street station, Cork. The Cork, Blackrock &amp; Passage Railway was not only one of the earliest railways in Ireland but also the only narrow gauge railway in the British Isles to have double track. \nThe railway closed in 1932 but the Albert Street terminus still stands and is used by a firm of builders merchants.",
