          "path": "_m/g/c/1/z/cork-blackrock-and-passage-railway-wp/monkstown-railway-station-site.jpg",
          "filename": "Monkstown railway station (site), County Cork (geograph 5963672).jpg",
          "caption": "Monkstown railway station (site), County CorkOpened in 1903 by the Cork Blackrock &amp; Passage Railway on its 3 foot gauge line from Cork to Crosshaven, this station closed in 1932.\nView north east towards Glenbrook and Cork. The old platform is a remarkable survivor, given that it saw its last passengers 86 years previously!",
          "alt": "Monkstown railway station (site), County CorkOpened in 1903 by the Cork Blackrock &amp; Passage Railway on its 3 foot gauge line from Cork to Crosshaven, this station closed in 1932.\nView north east towards Glenbrook and Cork. The old platform is a remarkable survivor, given that it saw its last passengers 86 years previously!",
